---
title: Diagrams
description: Eight diagram languages from fenced code blocks
---

# Diagrams

Carve draws from fenced code blocks. The diagram stays plain text in the source,
and a client library turns it into vector output. Eight languages ship as
presets of one extension.

## Mermaid

``` mermaid
flowchart LR
  S[".crv source"] --> P["carve-lang"]
  P --> H["HTML + Markdown headings"]
  H --> Z["Zensical build"]
  Z --> O["a page"]
```

``` mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  participant A as Author
  participant C as zensical-carve
  participant Z as Zensical
  A->>C: writes page.crv
  C->>C: renders Carve
  C->>Z: hands back headings and code as Markdown
  Z-->>A: a page with a table of contents
```

## Chart.js

``` chart
{
  "type": "bar",
  "data": {
    "labels": ["carve-rs", "carve-php", "carve-js", "carve-rb"],
    "datasets": [{
      "label": "downloads",
      "data": [69, 3860, 1683, 478],
      "backgroundColor": ["#2563eb", "#7c3aed", "#0891b2", "#dc2626"]
    }]
  },
  "options": { "plugins": { "legend": { "display": false } } }
}
```

The same numbers as the table on the Blocks page, drawn by Chart.js. This block
carries no caption on purpose: in carve-rs a caption currently disables the
preset and the diagram falls back to source (markup-carve/carve-rs#1151).
carve-js and carve-php render it correctly.

## Vega-Lite

``` vega-lite
{
  "$schema": "https://vega.github.io/schema/vega-lite/v5.json",
  "description": "Engine downloads",
  "data": { "values": [
    {"engine": "carve-rs", "downloads": 69},
    {"engine": "carve-php", "downloads": 3860},
    {"engine": "carve-js", "downloads": 1683},
    {"engine": "carve-rb", "downloads": 478}
  ]},
  "mark": "point",
  "encoding": {
    "x": {"field": "engine", "type": "nominal"},
    "y": {"field": "downloads", "type": "quantitative"}
  }
}
```

## D2

The language Zensical tracks as a change request. Carve ships it as a preset.

``` d2
source: .crv file
engine: carve-lang
site: Zensical

source -> engine: prepare
engine -> site: Markdown + HTML
```

## Graphviz

``` dot
digraph carve {
  rankdir=LR;
  node [shape=box, style=rounded];
  spec -> "carve-rs";
  spec -> "carve-php";
  spec -> "carve-js";
}
```

## The rest

WaveDrom for digital timing, ABC for musical notation, and PlantUML for the full
UML set are presets too. Each needs its own client library, so this page shows
the markup rather than pretending the drawing happened.

``` wavedrom
{ "signal": [{ "name": "clk", "wave": "p......" }, { "name": "data", "wave": "x.34.5x" }] }
```

``` abc
X:1
T:A scale
M:4/4
K:C
CDEF GABc |
```
